      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0013",
      "text": "Again, we’re told that all things are getting worse, but the facts don’t support this.",
      "start": 111.62,
      "end": 117.2,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.7,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0014",
      "text": "This does not mean that global warming is not real, or a problem, but the one-sided story of alarmism makes us lose focus.",
      "start": 117.2,
      "end": 125.03,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.05,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0015",
      "text": "If we want to help the world’s poor, who are the most threatened by natural disasters, it’s less about cutting carbon emissions than it is about pulling them out of poverty.",
      "start": 125.03,
      "end": 134.42,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.5,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0016",
      "text": "The best way to see this is to look at the world’s deaths from natural disasters over time.",
      "start": 134.42,
      "end": 139.48,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.04,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0017",
      "text": "In the Oxford University database for death rates from floods, extreme temperatures, droughts, and storms, the average in the first part of last century, was more than 130 dead every year per million people.",
      "start": 139.54,
      "end": 152.26,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 1.57,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
