      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0025",
      "text": "But the narrative that the world’s climate is changing from bad to worse is unhelpful alarmism that prevents us from focusing on smart solutions.",
      "start": 194.76,
      "end": 204.54,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.13,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0026",
      "text": "A well-meaning environmentalist might argue that, because climate change is a reality, why not ramp up the rhetoric and focus on the bad news to make sure the public understands its importance?",
      "start": 204.54,
      "end": 214.53,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.05,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0027",
      "text": "But that’s exactly what we’ve done for the past 20 years.",
      "start": 214.53,
      "end": 217.69,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.65,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0028",
      "text": "Yet despite dramatic headlines, apocalyptic documentaries and annual climate summits, carbon emissions continue to rise, especially in rapidly developing countries like India, China and many African nations.",
      "start": 217.69,
      "end": 230.71,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.72,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0029",
      "text": "Alarmism has encouraged the pursuit of a one-sided climate policy of trying to cut carbon emissions by subsidizing wind farms and solar panels.",
      "start": 230.71,
      "end": 239.45899999999997,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.82,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0030",
      "text": "Yet today, according to the International Energy Agency, only about 0.4% of global energy consumption comes from solar photovoltaics and windmills.",
      "start": 239.459,
      "end": 248.68,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 1.75,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0031",
      "text": "And even with exceptionally optimistic assumptions about future deployment of wind and solar, the International Energy Agency expects that these energy forms will provide a minuscule 2.2% of the world’s energy by 2040.",
      "start": 248.68,
      "end": 262.44,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 1.95,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0032",
      "text": "In other words, for at least the next two decades, solar and wind energy are simply expensive, feel-good measures that will have an imperceptible climate impact.",
      "start": 262.44,
      "end": 272.41,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 1.95,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0033",
      "text": "Instead, we should focus on investing in research and development of green energy to lower its costs, so everyone will want it, including China and India.",
      "start": 272.41,
      "end": 282.72,
      "screeningType": "score",
      "suspicionScore": 0.09,
      "reviewThreshold": 2,
      "suspectedIssue": false,
      "nextStep": "not_prioritized",
      "truthStatus": "not_assessed"
    },
    {
      "videoId": "3PWtaackIJU",
      "sentenceId": "s0034",
      "text": "We urgently need a more balanced climate conversation if we are to make sensible choices and pick the right climate policy that can actually help fix climate change.",
